# diagram.sketch render projection (authored): the layout of a w.diagram instance and what is drawn for it.
#
# Layout, all in rules. A node outside any group is a unit; a group with members is one unit whose members are set out
# inside it (row, column, grid, or the bars and points of a chart). Units flow top to bottom: an edge u -> v puts v
# on a lower level than u (the longest path from a unit with no incoming edge); an edge that closes a cycle (it goes
# to a unit made earlier that reaches back to it) does not count. Within a level the units keep the order of their
# first parent (a tree keeps its branches apart, so its edges do not cross), then the order they were made. Each level
# is a row, centred; rows are stacked with a gap between them. A pinned node or group stays where it was put.
#
# Edges are routed orthogonally through the gaps: an edge to the next level goes down into the gap under its source,
# across, and down into the top of its target; any other edge (skipping levels, going back up, or within a level) goes
# through the gap under its source to a lane right of every unit, along the lane and in through the gap above its
# target. Edges inside a group run in the gaps between its cells. So a routed edge crosses no node.
@dg.const.type core.type of=ui.diagram.const
@dg.base.type core.type of=ui.diagram.base
@dg.grade.type core.type of=ui.diagram.grade
@dg.textw.type core.type of=ui.diagram.textw
@dg.gridcols.type core.type of=ui.diagram.gridcols
@dg.pow.type core.type of=ui.diagram.pow
@dg.outline.type core.type of=ui.diagram.outline
@dg.colour.type core.type of=ui.diagram.colour
@dg.alias.type core.type of=ui.diagram.alias
@dg.size.type core.type of=ui.diagram.size
@dg.labelw.type core.type of=ui.diagram.labelw
@dg.lwidth.type core.type of=ui.diagram.lwidth
@dg.dim0.type core.type of=ui.diagram.dim0
@dg.dim.type core.type of=ui.diagram.dim
@dg.inside.type core.type of=ui.diagram.inside
@dg.unitof.type core.type of=ui.diagram.unitof
@dg.gorder.type core.type of=ui.diagram.gorder
@dg.unit.type core.type of=ui.diagram.unit
